QMacStyle: Size line edits and spin boxes like NSTextField under Liquid Glass

Not upstream: QMacStyle in the 6.10, 6.11 and 6.12 branches and in dev
(checked in November 2026) has no Liquid Glass heights for line edits
and spin boxes.

With Liquid Glass the bezel of an NSTextField shows 26, 24 and 21 pt
tall for the regular, small and mini control sizes: the text field is
24, 22 and 19 pt tall and its bezel reaches 1 pt beyond it at every
side. QMacStyle draws the bezel within the rect of a line edit, and kept
a line edit at 21, 18 and 18 pt, the heights of the old design, while a
spin box drew its edit field 1 pt inside its rect, so its bezel was only
19, 16 and 16 pt tall. A line edit or a spin box with a frame now gets
at least the height of the bezel of the NSTextField of its control size,
and the edit field of a spin box reaches the edges of the spin box, so
both look as tall as an AppKit text field next to them. The text stays
vertically centered, which puts it where AppKit has it, within half a
point. Frameless line edits, like the ones inside spin boxes and
editable combo boxes, are left as they are. Only Liquid Glass is
affected.

--- a/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
+++ b/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
@@ -362,6 +362,14 @@
     26, 22, 15
 };
 
+// Heights of the bezel of an NSTextField with Liquid Glass, one for each of
+// QStyleHelper::WidgetSizePolicy. The bezel reaches 1 pt beyond the frame of
+// the text field, which is 24, 22 and 19 pt tall, while QMacStyle draws it
+// within the rect of a line edit. The text stays vertically centered.
+static const int textFieldLiquidGlassHeight[3] = {
+    26, 24, 21
+};
+
 static const int toolButtonArrowSize = 7;
 static const int toolButtonArrowMargin = 2;
 
@@ -6568,6 +6576,10 @@
             }
             case SC_SpinBoxEditField:
                 ret = spin->rect.adjusted(fw, fw, -fw, -fw);
+                // With Liquid Glass the bezel of the edit field reaches the edges of the
+                // spin box, like the one of a QLineEdit (see CT_SpinBox)
+                if (qt_apple_runningWithLiquidGlass())
+                    ret = spin->rect;
                 if (spin->buttonSymbols != QAbstractSpinBox::NoButtons) {
                     ret.setWidth(spin->rect.width() - spinBoxSep - spinner_w);
                     ret = visualRect(spin->direction, spin->rect, ret);
@@ -6611,6 +6623,27 @@
             const bool hasButtons = (vopt->buttonSymbols != QAbstractSpinBox::NoButtons);
             const int buttonWidth = hasButtons ? proxy()->subControlRect(CC_SpinBox, vopt, SC_SpinBoxUp, widget).width() : 0;
             sz += QSize(buttonWidth, 0);
+            // The edit field is as tall as a QLineEdit next to it (see CT_LineEdit)
+            if (vopt->frame && qt_apple_runningWithLiquidGlass()) {
+                const auto size = d->effectiveAquaSizeConstrain(opt, widget);
+                sz.setHeight(qMax(sz.height(), textFieldLiquidGlassHeight[size]));
+            }
+        }
+        break;
+#endif
+#if QT_CONFIG(lineedit)
+    case CT_LineEdit:
+        sz = QCommonStyle::sizeFromContents(ct, opt, csz, widget);
+        // A line edit with a frame is drawn as a bezeled NSTextField, which is
+        // taller with Liquid Glass. Frameless ones, like those inside a spin box
+        // or an editable combo box, are left as they are.
+        if (qt_apple_runningWithLiquidGlass()) {
+            const auto *frame = qstyleoption_cast<const QStyleOptionFrame *>(opt);
+            if (frame && frame->lineWidth > 0) {
+                const auto size = d->effectiveAquaSizeConstrain(opt, widget, ct);
+                sz.setHeight(qMax(sz.height(), textFieldLiquidGlassHeight[size]));
+                useAquaGuideline = false;
+            }
         }
         break;
 #endif
